+## Bundles
+
+Two groups of endpoints are also sold as fixed monthly bundles, for teams that would rather
+commit than meter from zero. Both are available two ways, at identical per-call rates.
+
+### Core Identity Exposure, $150/mo
+
+Six endpoints answering one question: has this identity already been compromised?
+
+| Endpoint | Per call | What it answers |
+|---|---|---|
+| `/v1/metered/breach` | $0.10 | Does this address appear in breach corpora and dark web credential dumps? |
+| `/v1/metered/infostealer` | $0.50 | Were these credentials harvested by stealer malware? |
+| `/v1/metered/domain` | $0.30 | Is someone typosquatting this brand? |
+| `/v1/metered/oauth-watchlist` | $0.30 | Are OAuth or API tokens for this identity circulating? |
+| `/v1/metered/crypto-intel` | $0.30 | Is this wallet or domain in the criminal corpus? |
+| `/v1/metered/sim-swap` | $0.25 | Has this number been SIM swapped recently? |
+
+The six are designed to be correlated rather than used alone. An address in a breach corpus is
+routine; the same address with a fresh stealer-log hit and recent SIM swap activity is an active
+incident.
+
+**`sim-swap` currently returns `503`.** Carrier registration is in progress and the endpoint is
+not billed while it is unavailable. It is listed here because it is part of the bundle you are
+buying, not because it works today.
+
+- AWS Marketplace: [Core Identity Exposure API Bundle](https://aws.amazon.com/marketplace/pp/prodview-zgdxyqfd63hog)
+- Direct: `POST /developer/bundle-checkout` with `{"bundle": "a", "email": "you@example.com"}`
+
+### Agentic Attack Surface, $299/mo
+
+`tech-stack-cve`, `bulk-identity-risk`, `llm-credential-exposure`, `mcp-registry-risk` and
+`prompt-injection-breach`.
+
+- AWS Marketplace: [Consumption Security API Bundles](https://aws.amazon.com/marketplace/pp/prodview-6p6csngrcg3zq)
+- Direct: `POST /developer/bundle-checkout` with `{"bundle": "d", "email": "you@example.com"}`
+
+### Which door
+
+Buying through AWS Marketplace draws the spend down against your existing AWS commitment, so
+procurement sees a line item you have already committed to rather than a new vendor. If you do
+not have an AWS procurement relationship, the direct door is a card and takes a minute.
+
+Per-call rates are identical on both, by construction: a single price table in the API decides
+what a call costs, and each door bills that same number through its own rail. The monthly fee
+buys access to the bundle; calls are billed on top of it either way.
+
